---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {boundary,termsActive} from '../../lib/content-terms';
import {qualification} from '../../lib/build-profile';
import {pageHref} from '../../lib/routes';
---
<Layout title="Content terms" active="licensing"><div class="container"><header class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">CONTENT AND REUSE</p><h1>Content terms</h1><p class="lead">Separate terms for content, code and source.</p></header>
{!termsActive && <div class="draft-notice" role="note"><strong>{boundary.display_state}</strong><p>The owner has approved these content terms in substance. They remain not yet effective in this local review. A separately authorized public release is required to activate them. Existing artifact and third-party terms remain unchanged.</p></div>}
{qualification && <div class="draft-notice" role="note"><strong>Local qualification only</strong><p>This renders the public wording for inspection. It has no legal effect, publication act, or live indexing.</p></div>}
<div class="reading-layout"><article class="article"><section id="boundaries"><h2>Which layer is covered?</h2><dl class="license-layers">{boundary.layers.map(layer=><div id={layer.id}><dt>{layer.label}</dt><dd>{layer.treatment}</dd></div>)}</dl></section>
<section id="content-notice"><h2>Content copyright and permitted use</h2><p class="small-label">{qualification ? 'Public wording qualification; no effective date' : termsActive ? `Effective from ${boundary.effective_date}` : 'Not yet effective'}</p><div class="proposed-terms">{boundary.proposed_notice_paragraphs.map(p=><p>{p}</p>)}</div><p><a href={`${pageHref('annex')}#lfh-definition`}>About Lean for Human and declaration cards</a></p></section>
<section id="activation"><h2>{termsActive ? 'Publication record' : 'Publication activation is separate'}</h2>{qualification ? <p>This qualification has no legal effect. A separate owner act and actual public release are required.</p> : termsActive ? <p>These terms apply from the publication date shown above. Separate source and third-party licenses remain unchanged.</p> : <p>The permissions above have no new legal effect in this local review. They become the published content notice only through a separately authorized public release. No Creative Commons license is applied.</p>}<p>Mathematical ideas, facts, methods and results as such, and uses permitted by applicable law, remain outside these content restrictions.</p><p><a href="./boundary.json">Machine-readable content-terms status and boundaries</a></p></section></article><aside class="contents" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#boundaries">Content, code and source</a><a href="#content-notice">Content wording</a><a href="#activation">Publication activation</a></aside></div></div></Layout>
